WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090
1991.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.990
India's real growth was just 1.1 per cent.

3
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.230
Its economy almost stalled.

4
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:13.110
That year, the whole economy was
worth about 270 billion dollars.

5
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:18.090
By 2025, it was worth
3.96 trillion dollars:

6
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.410
about 14.6 times larger.

7
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:26.750
In 2025, India was home to
about 1.46 billion people.

8
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.450
So what changed?

9
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.310
How did a stalling economy become
one of the world's largest?

10
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.250
In this mission, you'll
measure how fast India grew,

11
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.370
and how the work people do has shifted.

12
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.270
Then you'll weigh up the
reasons, and ask who has gained,

13
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.950
and who has been left behind.

14
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.920
Your mission: explain what changed India's
economy after its near-stall in 1991.
